## 10. Acceptance command — the run that is owed

```bash
export GODOT=/Applications/Godot.app/Contents/MacOS/Godot
cd /Users/lucafantini/Desktop/Personal/Padel-3D/steam-circuit-padel-godot
"$GODOT" --headless --path godot/ --script res://tests/ui/pause_audit.gd ; echo "exit=$?"
```

Reading a run: the exit code is not a pass signal (a script that fails to parse also exits 0) —
the tally line `PASS n/n` / `FAIL n/n` and the `SCRIPT ERROR` count are the evidence. What a green
run prints: `PASS 163/163` … with the `# notes:` block naming the palette misses (§7), the
not-ported rows (§9), the theme parse error (§11) and the language-flip count. A FAIL names the
check; every check name is namespaced (`pause/…`) and greppable.

